export function referenceImagePrompt(boss) {
  return `MERIDIUS BOSS CONCEPT — ${boss.name.toUpperCase()}

REFERENCE ROLES: Image 1 controls painted shape language, the elevated three-quarter camera and cool shadow handling only. Image 2 controls the actual generated Higgsfield rendering: broad hand-painted forms, earthy material texture, warm lit planes and restrained edge detail only. Both are STYLE REFERENCES ONLY. Do not copy their locations, scenery, compositions, people, unit models, health bars, grids or overlays. ${boss.creatureReference ? 'Image 3 is a small creature-motif reference only: borrow the low elongated red crawler body and scuttling leg arrangement, then design a distinct colossal fungal boss. Do not copy its pixel resolution, exact anatomy, scenery or camera.' : 'There is no prescribed setting reference; design the environment described below.'}

ART DIRECTION: Detailed hand-painted fantasy tactics illustration matching the supplied Meridius art. Broad readable silhouettes with carefully grouped crisp brush shapes, warm muted highlights, cool deep green-blue shadows, weathered natural materials and controlled local contrast. Preserve painted texture rather than adding a pixelation filter. No glossy 3D, photorealism, plastic materials, thick comic outlines, extreme lens effects or depth-of-field blur. Adapt the colours to the creature and its new habitat, rather than forcing every scene to be green or golden.

SUBJECT AND NEW SETTING: ${boss.art}

SCALE AND READABILITY: ${boss.scale} Use the small company formations and environment as honest scale cues. The creature must feel overwhelmingly large, but the viewer must still distinguish its anatomy, the nearest threatened squad, reserve positions and the next open route. One boss only. No horde, independent minions or extra creatures. Company soldiers wear blue-and-cream clothing, simple steel equipment and restrained eagle-shield motifs. Do not copy any figures from the style references.

CAMERA AND LIGHT: Elevated three-quarter strategy-game view, near-parallel perspective, whole local encounter visible with generous margin around the main silhouette. A coherent upper-left light with legible material colour in the shadows. Any glow is local to the named creature feature and cannot obscure anatomy or ground. Convey drama through scale, pose and composition.

OUTPUT: One 16:9 landscape image, one composition, no collage, text, title, labels, HUD, grid, border, watermark, reference insets or swatches. This is an encounter concept illustration, not a final sprite or a rules diagram. Keep all essential body parts in frame, except the explicitly buried unseen body of the Crown. Do not add a magenta background. Image quality 2K is set in the website UI.`;
}

// Current pass: original concepts from the written descriptions (24 October).
// Keep referenceImagePrompt above as the editable record of the earlier approach.
export function imagePrompt(boss) {
  const art = boss.art
    .replace(' inspired only by the low scuttling reddish silhouette of the supplied small Drova reference', '')
    .replace(/ Style images control painting only and must not contribute their scenery\./g, '')
    .replace(/ No copied forest-road composition from the style references\./g, '')
    .replace(/ Use the supplied images for rendering style only, never their settings\./g, '');
  return [
    `MERIDIUS BOSS CONCEPT — ${boss.name.toUpperCase()}. Original design from this written brief; no image references.`,
    `CREATURE: ${boss.silhouette} ${boss.construction || ''}`.trim(),
    `COMPOSITION: ${art}`,
    `SCALE: ${boss.scale.split(';')[0]}. Exactly six tiny blue-and-cream human squads provide scale; they are separated formations, not six giant individuals. One boss only, no other creatures. Leave broad readable movement routes.`,
    'STYLE: Detailed hand-painted fantasy tactics illustration. Broad crisp brush shapes, textured natural materials, muted warm highlights and cool blue-green shadows. Elevated three-quarter strategy view with near-parallel perspective. Coherent upper-left light. Avoid glossy 3D, photorealism, heavy comic outlines and pixel filters.',
    'OUTPUT: One 16:9 landscape composition. Keep the whole essential silhouette in frame with generous margin; only the Crown’s buried body may remain underground. No text, labels, HUD, grid, border, watermark, collage or reference insets. This is concept artwork, not a final game asset.'
  ].join('\n\n');
}
